From 2fe5da6f27249f96843bbbf521a0c0e5a1b3b360 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:51:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/56] util/disk_cache: add a Horizon backend
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 7 item 1 (Mesa shader disk cache on Horizon)
Why: disk_cache_os.c is written against mmap, flock, fcntl(F_SETLK),
 posix_fallocate, ftw and getpwuid_r. Every one of them is absent on
 devkitA64's newlib, and they are not incidental to it: the multi-file
 backend is a directory of small files locked against other processes
 with an mmap'd index, which is the wrong shape for an SD card even
 where the calls exist. So Horizon replaces that one file, and keeps
 disk_cache.c — the key derivation, the put queue, the compression and
 the statistics are upstream's and are not worth reimplementing.

 The new backend is one append-only, CRC-validated file per GPU, held
 open for the life of the cache. There is no lock, because Horizon runs
 one homebrew title at a time; there is no rename, because rename() over
 an existing target fails on Horizon and because renaming is a path
 operation, which brings us to the constraint that shaped the rest:

   libnx routes every path-based devoptab entry point — open, stat,
   unlink, mkdir, rename, diropen — through fsdev_fixpath(), which
   copies into the single file-scope buffer __nx_dev_path_buf with no
   lock (nx/source/runtime/devices/fs_dev.c:211, and `char *fs_path =
   __nx_dev_path_buf` at 405, 1111, 1197, 1225 and 1276).

 disk_cache.c calls the backend from its put queue, i.e. off the calling
 thread, so a backend that did path work would be a data race whose
 symptom is a write to the wrong file. This one does none after it
 opens: the store works entirely through the handle, and compacts in
 place rather than through a temporary file.

 The store itself is horizon_gpu's blob cache, which lives outside Mesa
 because a format whose value is what it does with a *damaged* file has
 to be testable against damaged files — 138 host checks under ASan and
 UBSan cover truncation, flipped payload and header bytes, an
 interrupted compaction, a record claiming more than the file holds, a
 file from another driver build, and an empty one. Everything
 Mesa-shaped stays here: compression, the entry layout, and the driver
 keys blob, which is handed to the store as the identity it rejects a
 mismatched file by.

 Two smaller decisions are in this patch and are worth naming:

 - The put queue takes one thread here instead of four. The comment
   above it reasons about desktop CPUs and relies on
   UTIL_QUEUE_INIT_USE_MINIMUM_PRIORITY to keep the extra threads
   harmless — but that flag is implemented `#if defined(__linux__)`
   (u_queue.c:254 and 334), so on Horizon it does nothing, and four
   normal-priority threads would compete with a render loop on a console
   that gives homebrew three cores. They would serialise on the store's
   lock in any case.

 - put_key()/has_key() go to the backend rather than to the index.
   Upstream keeps those marks in an mmap'd 64 K-slot table where a
   collision silently overwrites; there is no mmap here, so the store
   records them instead, and disk_cache_mmap_cache_index() allocates
   only the eight bytes of size counter that remain meaningful — not the
   two megabytes of table, which would be 2 MiB of a 237 MiB applet-mode
   budget spent on an index nothing in NVK reads.

Evidence: measured on devkitA64 gcc 15.2.0 (newlib), cross-building the
 non-driver core with -Dshader-cache=enabled. Upstream's disk_cache_os.c
 is not built; disk_cache_horizon.c is:

   disk_cache.c.o             79968 bytes  42 defined symbols
   disk_cache_horizon.c.o     64024 bytes  53 defined symbols
   disk_cache_os.c.o          not built
   mesa_cache_db.c.o           1432 bytes   0 defined symbols
   compress.c.o                9840 bytes   7 defined symbols

 and libmesa_util.a no longer needs any of the calls the feature was
 turned off for:

   $ nm -u build/mesa-probe/src/util/libmesa_util.a | sort -u \
       | grep -E 'mmap|flock|posix_fallocate|memfd_create|getpwuid|nftw'
   (no output)

 The one remaining unresolved symbol of that family is `fcntl`, from
 os_file.c's os_create_anonymous_file, which predates this work and is
 unrelated to the cache.

 Configure reports zlib 1.3.1 and zstd through devkitPro's portlibs, so
 HAVE_COMPRESSION is defined and entries are deflated exactly as they
 are everywhere else.
Upstream: no — it is a platform backend, named for its platform. The
 parts that are not platform-specific were split out into the two
 patches before this one so that they can go upstream on their own.
---
 src/util/disk_cache.c         |  65 +++-
 src/util/disk_cache_horizon.c | 592 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/util/disk_cache_os.h      |  40 +++
 src/util/meson.build          |  39 ++-
 4 files changed, 733 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/util/disk_cache_horizon.c

diff --git a/src/util/disk_cache.c b/src/util/disk_cache.c
index 40bd6e58ea5..0e251f48cae 100644
--- a/src/util/disk_cache.c
+++ b/src/util/disk_cache.c
@@ -82,7 +82,17 @@ disk_cache_init_queue(struct disk_cache *cache)
     * The queue will resize automatically when it's full, so adding new jobs
     * doesn't stall.
     */
-   return util_queue_init(&cache->cache_queue, "disk$", 32, 4,
+   /* One thread on Horizon, not four. The reasoning above is about
+    * desktop CPUs, and it leans on UTIL_QUEUE_INIT_USE_MINIMUM_PRIORITY
+    * to make the extra threads harmless — but that flag is implemented
+    * only `#if defined(__linux__)` (u_queue.c), so here it does nothing
+    * and four normal-priority threads would compete with a render loop
+    * on a console that gives homebrew three cores. The backend is a
+    * single file behind a single lock, so extra threads would serialise
+    * on it in any case. */
+   unsigned num_threads = DETECT_OS_HORIZON ? 1 : 4;
+
+   return util_queue_init(&cache->cache_queue, "disk$", 32, num_threads,
                           UTIL_QUEUE_INIT_RESIZE_IF_FULL |
                           UTIL_QUEUE_INIT_USE_MINIMUM_PRIORITY |
                           UTIL_QUEUE_INIT_SET_FULL_THREAD_AFFINITY, NULL);
@@ -198,6 +208,19 @@ disk_cache_type_create(const char *gpu_name,
    /* Seed our rand function */
    s_rand_xorshift128plus(cache->seed_xorshift128plus, true);
 
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+   /* After the driver keys blob and not beside the other backends,
+    * because the store is handed that blob as the identity it refuses a
+    * mismatched file by, and it does not exist until here. */
+   if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON && !cache->path_init_failed &&
+       !disk_cache_horizon_open(cache)) {
+      util_queue_finish(&cache->cache_queue);
+      util_queue_destroy(&cache->cache_queue);
+      cache->path_init_failed = true;
+      cache->type = DISK_CACHE_NONE;
+   }
+#endif
+
    ralloc_free(local);
 
    return cache;
@@ -218,7 +241,12 @@ disk_cache_create(const char *gpu_name, const char *driver_id,
    uint64_t max_size = 0;
    const char *max_size_str;
 
-   if (debug_get_bool_option("MESA_DISK_CACHE_SINGLE_FILE", false)) {
+   if (DETECT_OS_HORIZON) {
+      /* The only backend this platform has; see disk_cache_horizon.c.
+       * The MESA_DISK_CACHE_* selectors below are not offered because
+       * the three backends they select cannot be built here. */
+      cache_type = DISK_CACHE_HORIZON;
+   } else if (debug_get_bool_option("MESA_DISK_CACHE_SINGLE_FILE", false)) {
       cache_type = DISK_CACHE_SINGLE_FILE;
    } else if (debug_get_bool_option("MESA_DISK_CACHE_DATABASE", false)) {
       cache_type = DISK_CACHE_DATABASE;
@@ -338,6 +366,10 @@ disk_cache_destroy(struct disk_cache *cache)
       if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_DATABASE)
          mesa_cache_db_multipart_close(&cache->cache_db);
 
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+      disk_cache_horizon_close(cache);
+#endif
+
       disk_cache_destroy_mmap(cache);
    }
 
@@ -358,6 +390,13 @@ disk_cache_remove(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
       return;
    }
 
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+   if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON) {
+      disk_cache_horizon_remove_item(cache, key);
+      return;
+   }
+#endif
+
    char *filename = disk_cache_get_cache_filename(cache, key);
    if (filename == NULL) {
       return;
@@ -453,6 +492,10 @@ cache_put(void *job, void *gdata, int thread_index)
       disk_cache_write_item_to_disk_foz(dc_job);
    } else if (dc_job->cache->type == DISK_CACHE_DATABASE) {
       disk_cache_db_write_item_to_disk(dc_job);
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+   } else if (dc_job->cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON) {
+      disk_cache_horizon_write_item_to_disk(dc_job);
+#endif
    } else if (dc_job->cache->type == DISK_CACHE_MULTI_FILE) {
       filename = disk_cache_get_cache_filename(dc_job->cache, dc_job->key);
       if (filename == NULL)
@@ -611,6 +654,10 @@ disk_cache_get(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key, size_t *size)
          buf = disk_cache_load_item_foz(cache, key, size);
       } else if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_DATABASE) {
          buf = disk_cache_db_load_item(cache, key, size);
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+      } else if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON) {
+         buf = disk_cache_horizon_load_item(cache, key, size);
+#endif
       } else if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_MULTI_FILE) {
          char *filename = disk_cache_get_cache_filename(cache, key);
          if (filename)
@@ -643,6 +690,15 @@ disk_cache_put_key(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
    if (cache->path_init_failed)
       return;
 
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+   /* There is no mmap here, so there is no shared key index to write
+    * into; the backend records the mark itself. */
+   if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON) {
+      disk_cache_horizon_put_key(cache, key);
+      return;
+   }
+#endif
+
    entry = &cache->stored_keys[i * CACHE_KEY_SIZE];
 
    memcpy(entry, key, CACHE_KEY_SIZE);
@@ -670,6 +726,11 @@ disk_cache_has_key(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
    if (cache->path_init_failed)
       return false;
 
+#if DETECT_OS_HORIZON
+   if (cache->type == DISK_CACHE_HORIZON)
+      return disk_cache_horizon_has_key(cache, key);
+#endif
+
    entry = &cache->stored_keys[i * CACHE_KEY_SIZE];
 
    return memcmp(entry, key, CACHE_KEY_SIZE) == 0;
diff --git a/src/util/disk_cache_horizon.c b/src/util/disk_cache_horizon.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..de215239dd2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/util/disk_cache_horizon.c
@@ -0,0 +1,592 @@
+/*
+ * Copyright © 2026 mesa-nvk-horizon contributors
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
+ */
+
+/*
+ * The OS half of the shader disk cache, for Horizon (Nintendo Switch).
+ *
+ * This file stands in for disk_cache_os.c, which cannot be built here:
+ * it is written against mmap, flock, fcntl(F_SETLK), posix_fallocate,
+ * ftw and getpwuid_r, and this C library (devkitA64's newlib) has none
+ * of them. The generic half — disk_cache.c: key derivation, the put
+ * queue, compression, the statistics — is upstream's and is used
+ * unchanged, which is the point of replacing only this file.
+ *
+ * Storage is horizon_gpu's blob cache (horizon_gpu/blob_cache.h): one
+ * append-only, CRC-validated file per GPU, holding opaque bytes. It
+ * lives outside Mesa because a format whose value is what it does with a
+ * damaged file has to be testable against damaged files, which is what
+ * this project's host test suite does to it. Everything Mesa-shaped —
+ * compression, the driver keys blob, the entry layout below — is here.
+ *
+ * WHAT AN ENTRY LOOKS LIKE. The blob cache stores bytes and asks no
+ * questions, so this file gives each entry a four-byte little-endian
+ * uncompressed length followed by the deflated payload. Nothing else is
+ * needed: the blob cache already checksums every record, and it already
+ * refuses a whole file whose driver key does not match, which is the
+ * check upstream's multi-file backend performs per entry by storing the
+ * driver keys blob inside each one.
+ *
+ * WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT IMPLEMENTED. The multi-file, Fossilize and
+ * Mesa-DB backends. A directory of small files is the wrong shape for an
+ * SD card, and the other two need flock. Their entry points are defined
+ * here because disk_cache.c refers to them, and each says no.
+ *
+ * THREADING. disk_cache.c calls into this file from its put queue, so
+ * every entry point that touches the store takes `cache->horizon_lock`.
+ * There is a second, less obvious rule: no path operation may happen off
+ * the thread that created the cache. libnx routes open/stat/unlink/
+ * mkdir/rename through one unlocked global path buffer, so a second
+ * thread doing path work corrupts the first one's path. Everything here
+ * respects that — the only path operations are the mkdir and the open in
+ * disk_cache_generate_cache_dir/disk_cache_horizon_open, both of which
+ * run inside disk_cache_create, and the blob cache performs none at all
+ * once it is open.
+ */
+
+#ifdef ENABLE_SHADER_CACHE
+
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <inttypes.h>
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <sys/types.h>
+
+#include "util/compress.h"
+#include "util/log.h"
+#include "util/os_misc.h"
+#include "util/ralloc.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
+
+#include "disk_cache.h"
+#include "disk_cache_os.h"
+
+#include "horizon_gpu/blob_cache.h"
+
+/* Where the cache goes when nothing overrides it.
+ *
+ * "sdmc:" is libnx's device name for the SD card, the only writable
+ * storage a homebrew title has by default. The directory name matches
+ * CACHE_DIR_NAME so that somebody looking at the card recognises it as
+ * the same thing Mesa writes everywhere else. */
+#define HORIZON_CACHE_ROOT "sdmc:/" CACHE_DIR_NAME
+
+/* Ceiling on the cache file.
+ *
+ * Upstream defaults to 1 GiB (disk_cache.c). That is a desktop number:
+ * this is a card that also holds somebody's games, and the environment
+ * variable that would normally lower it cannot be set on a console —
+ * libnx populates argv but not environ, so getenv() answers NULL for
+ * everything. 64 MiB is the compiled-in answer instead. It is roughly
+ * two orders of magnitude more than the shaders of anything this driver
+ * runs today, and it is small enough that nobody has to think about it. */
+#define HORIZON_CACHE_MAX_SIZE (UINT64_C(64) * 1024 * 1024)
+
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/* One store per file, however many caches ask for it                */
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* WHY THIS EXISTS. disk_cache_create() is called per physical device
+ * per instance, and every one of them on this GPU resolves to the same
+ * path. Two stores over one file is not a race that locking inside each
+ * of them can fix: each keeps its own append offset and its own index,
+ * so both append at what each believes is the end and the second
+ * overwrites the first, whose index then points at somebody else's
+ * record. Compaction makes it worse — one handle rewrites the file the
+ * other is indexing.
+ *
+ * It would not have returned a *wrong shader*: disk_cache_horizon_load_item
+ * goes through horizon_gpu_blob_cache_get(), which re-reads the record
+ * header and compares the key before it believes the index. So the
+ * failure mode was a cache that quietly stopped working rather than one
+ * that lied. That is still a defect, and the fix is the ordinary one —
+ * open each path once and hand out references.
+ *
+ * The lock is inside the reference and not in `struct disk_cache`,
+ * because it is the *store* that must be serialised, not the cache
+ * object: two caches sharing a store share its lock. */
+struct horizon_store_ref {
+   char *path;
+   horizon_gpu_blob_cache *store;
+   unsigned refcount;
+   simple_mtx_t lock;
+   struct horizon_store_ref *next;
+};
+
+static simple_mtx_t horizon_registry_lock = SIMPLE_MTX_INITIALIZER;
+static struct horizon_store_ref *horizon_registry;
+
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/* Lifecycle                                                         */
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+bool
+disk_cache_enabled(void)
+{
+   /* No __normal_user() question to ask: Horizon has no setuid, and a
+    * homebrew title runs as itself. What can be asked is whether the
+    * user turned it off. */
+   if (debug_get_bool_option("MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE",
+#ifdef SHADER_CACHE_DISABLE_BY_DEFAULT
+                             true
+#else
+                             false
+#endif
+                             ))
+      return false;
+
+   return true;
+}
+
+/* Returns the path of the cache *file*, not of a directory.
+ *
+ * Horizon keeps one file per GPU rather than a tree, so there is no
+ * per-cache subdirectory to make and nothing for the name to encode
+ * beyond the GPU: a driver change is caught by the driver key inside the
+ * file, which resets it in place. That is deliberately not done by
+ * putting the driver id in the file name — that would leave the previous
+ * build's file behind on the card, and reclaiming it would mean reading
+ * the directory and unlinking, i.e. two more path operations for no gain.
+ */
+const char *
+disk_cache_generate_cache_dir(void *mem_ctx, const char *gpu_name,
+                              const char *driver_id,
+                              const char *cache_dir_name_custom,
+                              enum disk_cache_type cache_type,
+                              bool mkdir_cache)
+{
+   const char *root = os_get_option("MESA_SHADER_CACHE_DIR");
+
+   if (root == NULL)
+      root = HORIZON_CACHE_ROOT;
+
+   if (mkdir_cache && mkdir(root, 0755) == -1 && errno != EEXIST) {
+      mesa_logw("disk cache: cannot create %s (%s); cache disabled",
+                root, strerror(errno));
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
+   return ralloc_asprintf(mem_ctx, "%s/%s.%s", root, gpu_name,
+                          cache_dir_name_custom != NULL
+                             ? cache_dir_name_custom
+                             : "hzc");
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_horizon_open(struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   const horizon_gpu_blob_cache_config config = {
+      .path = cache->path,
+      /* The identity is exactly what disk_cache_compute_key() hashes
+       * into every key: CACHE_VERSION, the driver id, the GPU name, the
+       * pointer size and the driver flags. Handing the store the same
+       * blob means a file written by a driver that would compute
+       * different keys is rejected as a whole rather than producing
+       * misses one entry at a time. */
+      .driver_key = cache->driver_keys_blob,
+      .driver_key_size = cache->driver_keys_blob_size,
+      .max_size = HORIZON_CACHE_MAX_SIZE,
+      .read_only = false,
+   };
+   horizon_gpu_blob_cache *store = NULL;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+
+   /* Already open for this path? Share it. */
+   for (struct horizon_store_ref *ref = horizon_registry; ref != NULL;
+        ref = ref->next) {
+      if (strcmp(ref->path, cache->path) == 0) {
+         ref->refcount++;
+         cache->horizon_ref = ref;
+         simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+         mesa_logi("disk cache: %s, shared with %u other cache object(s)",
+                   cache->path, ref->refcount - 1);
+         return true;
+      }
+   }
+
+   horizon_gpu_result r = horizon_gpu_blob_cache_open(&config, &store);
+   if (horizon_gpu_failed(r)) {
+      simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+      mesa_logw("disk cache: cannot open %s (%s); cache disabled",
+                cache->path, horizon_gpu_status_str(r.status));
+      return false;
+   }
+
+   horizon_gpu_blob_cache_stats st;
+   horizon_gpu_blob_cache_get_stats(store, &st);
+   if (st.was_reset)
+      mesa_logi("disk cache: %s did not match this driver build or could "
+                "not be read; started over (%" PRIu64 " bytes discarded)",
+                cache->path, st.discarded_bytes);
+   else if (st.was_truncated)
+      mesa_logi("disk cache: %s had an incomplete tail; %" PRIu64 " bytes "
+                "discarded, %u entries kept", cache->path,
+                st.discarded_bytes, st.entries);
+   else
+      mesa_logi("disk cache: %s, %u entries", cache->path, st.entries);
+
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = calloc(1, sizeof(*ref));
+   char *path_copy = ref != NULL ? strdup(cache->path) : NULL;
+   if (ref == NULL || path_copy == NULL) {
+      free(ref);
+      free(path_copy);
+      horizon_gpu_blob_cache_close(store);
+      simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+      mesa_logw("disk cache: out of memory registering %s; cache disabled",
+                cache->path);
+      return false;
+   }
+
+   ref->path = path_copy;
+   ref->store = store;
+   ref->refcount = 1;
+   simple_mtx_init(&ref->lock, mtx_plain);
+   ref->next = horizon_registry;
+   horizon_registry = ref;
+
+   cache->horizon_ref = ref;
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+   return true;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_horizon_close(struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return;
+
+   cache->horizon_ref = NULL;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+   if (--ref->refcount > 0) {
+      simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+      return;
+   }
+
+   for (struct horizon_store_ref **pp = &horizon_registry; *pp != NULL;
+        pp = &(*pp)->next) {
+      if (*pp == ref) {
+         *pp = ref->next;
+         break;
+      }
+   }
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&horizon_registry_lock);
+
+   horizon_gpu_blob_cache_close(ref->store);
+   simple_mtx_destroy(&ref->lock);
+   free(ref->path);
+   free(ref);
+}
+
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/* Entries                                                           */
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* Four bytes of uncompressed length, little-endian, ahead of the
+ * deflated payload. Written and read a byte at a time so the layout does
+ * not depend on this compiler's alignment rules. */
+#define HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX 4u
+
+void *
+disk_cache_horizon_load_item(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key,
+                             size_t *size)
+{
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return NULL;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&ref->lock);
+   void *raw = NULL;
+   size_t raw_size = 0;
+   horizon_gpu_result r =
+      horizon_gpu_blob_cache_get(ref->store, key, &raw, &raw_size);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&ref->lock);
+
+   if (horizon_gpu_failed(r))
+      return NULL;
+
+   if (raw_size < HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX) {
+      free(raw);
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
+   const uint8_t *p = raw;
+   uint32_t uncompressed = (uint32_t)p[0] | ((uint32_t)p[1] << 8) |
+                           ((uint32_t)p[2] << 16) | ((uint32_t)p[3] << 24);
+
+   /* The store checksums what it returns, so this cannot be a corrupt
+    * length — but it can be one written by a version of this file that
+    * laid entries out differently, so it is still bounded before it
+    * becomes an allocation. */
+   if (uncompressed == 0 || uncompressed > (64u * 1024 * 1024)) {
+      free(raw);
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
+   uint8_t *out = malloc(uncompressed);
+   if (out == NULL) {
+      free(raw);
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
+   if (!util_compress_inflate(p + HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX,
+                              raw_size - HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX, out,
+                              uncompressed)) {
+      free(out);
+      free(raw);
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
+   free(raw);
+
+   if (size != NULL)
+      *size = uncompressed;
+
+   return out;
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_horizon_write_item_to_disk(struct disk_cache_put_job *dc_job)
+{
+   struct disk_cache *cache = dc_job->cache;
+
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return false;
+   if (dc_job->size == 0 || dc_job->size > UINT32_MAX)
+      return false;
+
+   size_t max = util_compress_max_compressed_len(dc_job->size);
+   uint8_t *entry = malloc(max + HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX);
+   if (entry == NULL)
+      return false;
+
+   entry[0] = (uint8_t)(dc_job->size & 0xFFu);
+   entry[1] = (uint8_t)((dc_job->size >> 8) & 0xFFu);
+   entry[2] = (uint8_t)((dc_job->size >> 16) & 0xFFu);
+   entry[3] = (uint8_t)((dc_job->size >> 24) & 0xFFu);
+
+   size_t compressed = util_compress_deflate(dc_job->data, dc_job->size,
+                                             entry + HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX,
+                                             max);
+   if (compressed == 0) {
+      free(entry);
+      return false;
+   }
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&ref->lock);
+   horizon_gpu_result r =
+      horizon_gpu_blob_cache_put(ref->store, dc_job->key, entry,
+                                 compressed + HORIZON_ENTRY_PREFIX);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&ref->lock);
+
+   free(entry);
+
+   if (horizon_gpu_failed(r)) {
+      mesa_logw("disk cache: storing an entry failed (%s)",
+                horizon_gpu_status_str(r.status));
+      return false;
+   }
+
+   return true;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_horizon_remove_item(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
+{
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&ref->lock);
+   (void)horizon_gpu_blob_cache_remove(ref->store, key);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&ref->lock);
+}
+
+/* disk_cache.c keeps the put_key()/has_key() marks in an mmap'd index
+ * file, which is the one thing about this cache that cannot be done
+ * here at all. The store keeps them as records of their own instead —
+ * a strictly stronger promise than upstream's fixed 64 K-slot table,
+ * which loses a mark to a collision without saying so. */
+void
+disk_cache_horizon_put_key(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
+{
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&ref->lock);
+   (void)horizon_gpu_blob_cache_put_key(ref->store, key);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&ref->lock);
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_horizon_has_key(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
+{
+   struct horizon_store_ref *ref = cache->horizon_ref;
+
+   if (ref == NULL)
+      return false;
+
+   simple_mtx_lock(&ref->lock);
+   bool found = horizon_gpu_blob_cache_has_key(ref->store, key);
+   simple_mtx_unlock(&ref->lock);
+
+   return found;
+}
+
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+/* The backends Horizon does not have                                */
+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------- */
+
+/* Each of these exists because disk_cache.c names it. None is reachable:
+ * disk_cache_create() selects DISK_CACHE_HORIZON on this platform and
+ * the multi-file, Fossilize and Mesa-DB paths are never taken. They
+ * return "no" rather than assert, so that a future disk_cache.c which
+ * reached one would degrade to a cache miss instead of aborting a
+ * driver on a games console. */
+
+bool
+disk_cache_mmap_cache_index(void *mem_ctx, struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   /* Upstream maps 8 bytes of total-size counter followed by a 64 K-slot
+    * key table out of a file, and both are used through pointers into
+    * that mapping. There is no mmap here, and the 2 MiB table would be
+    * two megabytes of a 237 MiB applet-mode budget spent on an index
+    * nothing in NVK reads — so only the counter is allocated, and
+    * disk_cache.c's put_key()/has_key() go to the store instead. */
+   cache->index_mmap = rzalloc_size(cache, sizeof(uint64_t));
+   if (cache->index_mmap == NULL)
+      return false;
+
+   cache->index_mmap_size = sizeof(uint64_t);
+   cache->size = (p_atomic_uint64_t *)cache->index_mmap;
+   cache->stored_keys = NULL;
+
+   return true;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_destroy_mmap(struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   ralloc_free(cache->index_mmap);
+   cache->index_mmap = NULL;
+   cache->index_mmap_size = 0;
+   cache->size = NULL;
+   cache->stored_keys = NULL;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_touch_cache_user_marker(char *path)
+{
+   /* Upstream stamps a marker file so a system cleaner can tell when the
+    * cache was last used. Horizon has no such cleaner, and writing the
+    * marker would be another path operation for nobody. */
+   (void)path;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_delete_old_cache(void)
+{
+}
+
+char *
+disk_cache_get_cache_filename(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+   (void)key;
+   return NULL;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_evict_lru_item(struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_evict_item(struct disk_cache *cache, char *filename)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+   free(filename);
+}
+
+void *
+disk_cache_load_item(struct disk_cache *cache, char *filename, size_t *size)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+   (void)size;
+   free(filename);
+   return NULL;
+}
+
+void
+disk_cache_write_item_to_disk(struct disk_cache_put_job *dc_job,
+                              char *filename)
+{
+   (void)dc_job;
+   (void)filename;
+}
+
+void *
+disk_cache_load_item_foz(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key,
+                         size_t *size)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+   (void)key;
+   (void)size;
+   return NULL;
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_write_item_to_disk_foz(struct disk_cache_put_job *dc_job)
+{
+   (void)dc_job;
+   return false;
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_load_cache_index_foz(void *mem_ctx, struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   (void)mem_ctx;
+   (void)cache;
+   return false;
+}
+
+void *
+disk_cache_db_load_item(struct disk_cache *cache, const cache_key key,
+                        size_t *size)
+{
+   (void)cache;
+   (void)key;
+   (void)size;
+   return NULL;
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_db_write_item_to_disk(struct disk_cache_put_job *dc_job)
+{
+   (void)dc_job;
+   return false;
+}
+
+bool
+disk_cache_db_load_cache_index(void *mem_ctx, struct disk_cache *cache)
+{
+   (void)mem_ctx;
+   (void)cache;
+   return false;
+}
